IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART VII, "Transitional Provisions and Coming into Force": regs 94 to 95.
-- Text: the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (SOR-96-332.txt, lines 1724-1756);
-- an unofficial conversion, not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT IT DOES. Regs 94 to 94.4 carried the change from counting WEEKS of insurable employment to counting HOURS (effective
-- 5 January 1997): which provisions read "hours" as "weeks" until then, how many hours a pre-1997 week stands for (35), how pre-1997
-- weeks are placed and their earnings counted, and what happens to the last pay period of 1996. Reg 95 fixes when the
-- Regulations, and some of their provisions, came into force, and the periods in which the interim provisions of Schedule III apply.
-- The dates are carried as DATA (the brief's "Dates are data"): reg 95 is not commencement machinery here, because it says when
-- the interim provisions of Schedule III apply, and those rules are gated on it.
--
-- WHAT IS TAKEN AS AN INPUT. The facts about the claim (the day the benefit period was established, the hours worked, the pay
-- periods) are the person's. Sections 7 and 12 of the Act, regs 35, 37, 56 and 88 and section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance
-- Regulations are other provisions that these regs only re-read; nothing here restates them.
-- Past, but not spent in law: a benefit period established after 4 January 1997 may rest on employment before 1997, so these rules
-- are still the answer for such a claim; the rules take the dates as facts.

§ `reg 95 -- coming into force (dates as data)`

-- src:1750 | 95 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this Part, these Regulations come into force on June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(1) (src:1750)
`reg 95(1) the day on which these Regulations come into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30

-- src:1751 | (1.1) Sections 10 to 12 come into force on January 1, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(1.1) (src:1751)
`reg 95(1.1) the day on which sections 10 to 12 come into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 1997 1 1

-- src:1752 | (2) Sections 19 to 21 come into force on January 1, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(2) (src:1752)
`reg 95(2) the day on which sections 19 to 21 come into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 1997 1 1

-- src:1753 | (3) Sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) come into force on January 5, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(3) (src:1753)
`reg 95(3) the day on which sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) come into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 1997 1 5

-- The provisions that have a day of coming into force of their own, and "any other provision" (subsection (1) "Except as otherwise provided in this Part").
DECLARE `er6 Provision with a day of coming into force` IS ONE OF
    `er6 sections 10 to 12`
    `er6 sections 19 to 21`
    `er6 sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c)`
    `er6 any other provision of these Regulations`

-- src:1750 | 95 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this Part, these Regulations come into force on June 30, 1996.
-- src:1751 | (1.1) Sections 10 to 12 come into force on January 1, 1997.
-- src:1752 | (2) Sections 19 to 21 come into force on January 1, 1997.
-- src:1753 | (3) Sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) come into force on January 5, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(1) to (3) (src:1750-1753)
GIVEN provision IS AN `er6 Provision with a day of coming into force`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95 the provision is in force on the day` IF
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `er6 sections 10 to 12` THEN day AT LEAST `reg 95(1.1) the day on which sections 10 to 12 come into force`
    WHEN `er6 sections 19 to 21` THEN day AT LEAST `reg 95(2) the day on which sections 19 to 21 come into force`
    WHEN `er6 sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c)` THEN day AT LEAST `reg 95(3) the day on which sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) come into force`
    WHEN `er6 any other provision of these Regulations` THEN day AT LEAST `reg 95(1) the day on which these Regulations come into force`

-- src:1754 | (4) The provision set out in Part I of Schedule III applies during the period beginning on June 30, 1996 and ending on December 31, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(4) (src:1754)
`reg 95(4) the period in which the provision set out in Part I of Schedule III applies` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30
        `last day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1996 12 31

-- src:1755 | (4.1) The provision set out in Part I.1 of Schedule III applies in place of section 12 listed in subsection (1.1) during the period beginning on September 12, 1996 and ending on December 31, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(4.1) (src:1755)
`reg 95(4.1) the period in which the provision set out in Part I.1 of Schedule III applies in place of section 12` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1996 9 12
        `last day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1996 12 31

-- "from June 30, 1996 until the coming into force of those provisions": the interim provision applies up to the day before the
-- provision it replaces comes into force (fork F-95-5-UNTIL in NOTES.md).
-- src:1756 | (5) The provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of the provisions listed in subsections (2) and (3) from June 30, 1996 until the coming into force of those provisions.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(5) with reg 95(2) (src:1752) (src:1756)
`reg 95(5) the period in which Part II of Schedule III applies in place of the provisions listed in subsection (2)` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30
        `last day of the period` IS `reg 95(2) the day on which sections 19 to 21 come into force` MINUS 1

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(5) with reg 95(3) (src:1753) (src:1756)
`reg 95(5) the period in which Part II of Schedule III applies in place of the provisions listed in subsection (3)` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30
        `last day of the period` IS `reg 95(3) the day on which sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) come into force` MINUS 1

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(4) (src:1754)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(4) the provision set out in Part I of Schedule III applies on the day` IF
    `the day` day `falls within` `reg 95(4) the period in which the provision set out in Part I of Schedule III applies`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(4.1) (src:1755)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(4.1) the provision set out in Part I.1 of Schedule III applies in place of section 12 on the day` IF
    `the day` day `falls within` `reg 95(4.1) the period in which the provision set out in Part I.1 of Schedule III applies in place of section 12`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(5) (src:1756)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` IF
    `the day` day `falls within` `reg 95(5) the period in which Part II of Schedule III applies in place of the provisions listed in subsection (2)`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 95(5) (src:1756)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` IF
    `the day` day `falls within` `reg 95(5) the period in which Part II of Schedule III applies in place of the provisions listed in subsection (3)`

§ `reg 94 -- "hours" read as "weeks" until 4 January 1997`

-- src:1727 | 94 During the period beginning on June 30, 1996 and ending on January 4, 1997, a reference to "hours" in each of the following provisions shall be read as a reference to "weeks", with such modifications as the circumstances require:
-- src:1728 | (a) subsection 35(3);
-- src:1729 | (b) paragraph 35(7)(e);
-- src:1730 | (c) subparagraph 37(2)(c)(ii);
-- src:1731 | (d) subparagraph 56(2)(b)(iv);
-- src:1732 | (e) section 88; and
-- src:1733 | (f) subsection 93(5).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94 (src:1727-1733)
DECLARE `er6 Provision in which reg 94 reads hours as weeks` IS ONE OF
    `er6 subsection 35(3)`
    `er6 paragraph 35(7)(e)`
    `er6 subparagraph 37(2)(c)(ii)`
    `er6 subparagraph 56(2)(b)(iv)`
    `er6 section 88`
    `er6 subsection 93(5)`

DECLARE `er6 Unit in which a count is read` IS ONE OF
    `er6 hours`
    `er6 weeks`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94 (src:1727-1733)
`reg 94 the period in which a reference to hours is read as a reference to weeks` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30
        `last day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 1997 1 4

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94 (src:1727-1733)
GIVEN provision IS AN `er6 Provision in which reg 94 reads hours as weeks`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94 a reference to hours in the provision is read as a reference to weeks on the day` IF
        elem provision (LIST `er6 subsection 35(3)`, `er6 paragraph 35(7)(e)`, `er6 subparagraph 37(2)(c)(ii)`, `er6 subparagraph 56(2)(b)(iv)`, `er6 section 88`, `er6 subsection 93(5)`)
    AND `the day` day `falls within` `reg 94 the period in which a reference to hours is read as a reference to weeks`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94 (src:1727-1733)
GIVEN provision IS AN `er6 Provision in which reg 94 reads hours as weeks`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `er6 Unit in which a count is read`
DECIDE `reg 94 the unit in which the provision counts on the day` IS
    IF `reg 94 a reference to hours in the provision is read as a reference to weeks on the day` provision day
    THEN `er6 weeks`
    ELSE `er6 hours`

§ `reg 94.1 -- a week before 1997 stands for 35 hours`

-- src:1734 | 94.1 Where, for the purposes of the Act and in respect of a benefit period established on or after January 5, 1997, a claimant presents evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997, that week of insurable employment shall be considered to represent 35 hours of insurable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.1 (src:1734)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant presents evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94.1 the section applies to the claim` IF
        `the day on which the benefit period was established` AT LEAST YearMonthDay 1997 1 5
    AND `the claimant presents evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997`

-- NOTHING means the section does not apply, so the hours of the week are what the Act and the Regulations otherwise make them.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.1 (src:1734)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant presents evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 94.1 the hours of insurable employment that the week is considered to represent` IS
    IF `reg 94.1 the section applies to the claim` `the day on which the benefit period was established` `the claimant presents evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997`
    THEN JUST 35
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `reg 94.2 -- how the pre-1997 weeks are placed, and the earnings counted`

-- src:1735 | 94.2 Where, for the purposes of the Act and in respect of a benefit period established on or after January 5, 1997, a claimant presents evidence of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997,
-- src:1736 | (a) the weeks of insurable employment shall be considered to fall consecutively backward beginning on whichever of the following days occurred first:
-- src:1737 | (i) the last day of the last pay period in 1996, and
-- src:1738 | (ii) the last day of remunerated insurable employment if that day falls before the last pay period in 1996; and
-- src:1739 | (b) if the number of weeks of insurable employment is
-- src:1740 | (i) 20 or less, the insurable earnings are considered to be for that number of weeks, and
-- src:1741 | (ii) greater than 20, the insurable earnings are considered to be for the last 20 weeks in the period of employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.2 (src:1735-1741)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant presents evidence of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94.2 the section applies to the claim` IF
        `the day on which the benefit period was established` AT LEAST YearMonthDay 1997 1 5
    AND `the claimant presents evidence of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997`

-- (a) the weeks "fall consecutively backward beginning on whichever of the following days occurred first": (i) the last day of the
-- last pay period in 1996, and (ii) the last day of remunerated insurable employment if that day falls before the last pay period in 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.2(a) (src:1735-1738)
GIVEN `the last day of the last pay period in 1996` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the last pay period in 1996` IS A DATE
      `the last day of remunerated insurable employment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 94.2(a) the day from which the weeks of insurable employment fall consecutively backward` IS
    IF `the last day of remunerated insurable employment` LESS THAN `the first day of the last pay period in 1996`
    THEN `the last day of remunerated insurable employment`
    ELSE `the last day of the last pay period in 1996`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.2(b) (src:1739-1741)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of insurable employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 94.2(b) the number of weeks for which the insurable earnings are considered to be` IS
    IF `the number of weeks of insurable employment` AT MOST 20
    THEN `the number of weeks of insurable employment`
    ELSE 20

§ `reg 94.3 -- the last pay period beginning in December 1996`

-- src:1742 | 94.3 For the purpose of providing for the transition from weeks of insurable employment to hours of insurable employment where the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid to an insured person by their employer on or after January 1, 1997,
-- src:1743 | (a) the employer shall assess the insurability of the employment of that final pay period under these Regulations as they read on January 1, 1997; and
-- src:1744 | (b) the claimant shall, for the purposes of sections 7 and 12 of the Act, be determined to have worked in insurable employment for the greater of
-- src:1745 | (i) the number of hours provided for by section 94.1, and
-- src:1746 | (ii) the number of hours actually worked in each week or part of a week of insurable employment, of the final pay period, that falls in 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.3 (src:1742-1746)
GIVEN `the day on which the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94.3 the section applies to the pay period` IF
    `the day on which the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid` AT LEAST YearMonthDay 1997 1 1

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.3(a) (src:1743)
GIVEN `the day on which the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 94.3(a) the day as at which the employer reads these Regulations to assess the insurability of the employment of the final pay period` IS
    IF `reg 94.3 the section applies to the pay period` `the day on which the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid`
    THEN JUST (YearMonthDay 1997 1 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (b) "the greater of (i) the number of hours provided for by section 94.1, and (ii) the number of hours actually worked in each week
-- or part of a week of the final pay period that falls in 1996": read week by week (fork F-94-3 in NOTES.md); each such week counts for the
-- greater of 35 hours and the hours actually worked in it.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.3(b) (src:1744-1746)
GIVEN `the day on which the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid` IS A DATE
      `the hours actually worked in each week or part of a week of the final pay period that falls in 1996` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 94.3(b) the hours of insurable employment that the claimant is determined to have worked in the final pay period` IS
    IF `reg 94.3 the section applies to the pay period` `the day on which the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid`
    THEN JUST (sum (map (GIVEN h YIELD IF h GREATER THAN 35 THEN h ELSE 35) `the hours actually worked in each week or part of a week of the final pay period that falls in 1996`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `reg 94.4 -- section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations`

-- src:1747 | 94.4 Where, after January 5, 1997, section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations, as it read on June 29, 1996, applies and where the application of that section requires the consideration of insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier, section 94.1 of these Regulations shall be applied to convert those weeks in 1996 or earlier into hours and the number of weeks stipulated by paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations shall be converted into an hourly equivalent by multiplying the number of weeks required by 35.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.4 (src:1747)
GIVEN `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies` IS A DATE
      `its application requires the consideration of insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94.4 the section applies` IF
        `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies` GREATER THAN YearMonthDay 1997 1 5
    AND `its application requires the consideration of insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier`

-- Two conversions, both at 35 hours to the week: the insured weeks in 1996 or earlier go through section 94.1, and the number of weeks
-- that paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations stipulate is multiplied by 35.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.4 (src:1747)
GIVEN `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies` IS A DATE
      `its application requires the consideration of insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks to convert` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 94.4 the hours that the weeks of insurable employment are converted into` IS
    IF `reg 94.4 the section applies` `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies` `its application requires the consideration of insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier`
    THEN JUST (`the number of weeks to convert` TIMES 35)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 94.4 (src:1747)
GIVEN `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies` IS A DATE
      `its application requires the consideration of insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks required by paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 94.4 the hourly equivalent of the number of weeks stipulated by paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b)` IS
    IF `reg 94.4 the section applies` `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies` `its application requires the consideration of insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier`
    THEN JUST (`the number of weeks required by paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b)` TIMES 35)
    ELSE NOTHING
